<report>
<line><title>Mann-Whitney U test</title></line>
<line></line>
<line>Observations (x) in <in>sample_1</in> = <in>obs_1</in>   median = <in>median_1</in>   rank sum = <in>ranksum</in></line>
<line>Observations (y) in <in>sample_2</in> = <in>obs_2</in>   median = <in>median_2</in></line>
<line>U = <in>u</in>      U' = <in>u_prime</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><in>stats</in></line>
<line><pval>Lower side <in>p_l</in></pval> (H<sub>1</sub>: x tends to be less than y)</line>
<line><pval>Upper side <in>p_u</in></pval> (H<sub>1</sub>: x tends to be greater than y)</line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>p_2</in></pval> (H<sub>1</sub>: x tends to be distributed differently to y)</line>
<line></line>
<line>Theta (U'/mn) = <in>theta</in> <ci>(<in>pc0</in>% CI: <in>tll</in> to <in>tul</in>)</ci></line>
<line></line>
<block name="noconf">
<line>confidence interval not calculated if n1 or n2 </line>
</block>
<block name="conf">
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for difference between medians or means:</ci></line>
<line>Median difference = <in>median</in> <ci>(CI: <in>from</in> to <in>to</in>)</ci></line>
</block>
</report>
